<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Comparison of Transformer-based and MLP-based fusion between visual and textual features. While the Transformer-based fusion achieved competitive results, the MLP-based fusion demonstrated better performance in <span id="A6.T6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Desc.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To investigate potential limitations in expressivity, we conducted experiments on the comparison of Transformer-based and MLP-based fusion between visual and textual features.
Table <a href="#A6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix F Fusion of Visual and Textual Features ‣ Vela: An LLM-Hybrid-as-a-Judge Approachfor Evaluating Long Image Captions" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows the results of the variant modified to employ Transformer-based fusion.
The results demonstrate that the Transformer-based fusion achieved performance comparable to the MLP-based fusion overall, with slightly lower scores in <span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Desc</span>.
Given these results and the computational cost, we adopted MLP-based fusion in the final model.</p>
</div>
</section>
